      },
      "message": "fix(ui): the post list finds the selected post by name\n\nThe post combo filters the shipped posts by the post folder scan, but\nit still mapped the default post (PostRef::Builtin) to entry 0 and read\nnames[i]. An empty or unreadable post folder made the Setup Post page\npanic on each frame. A removed first post made the combo show another\npost as selected, while the label and script_of used the first post.\n\nThe new post_pick module finds the document's post by name\n(posting::post_name) in the filtered list and never indexes past it. A\npost whose file is gone shows its own name with \"(file missing)\", and\nthe document's post does not change. The page shows why the post\nfolder did not read (FolderScan::problem). The doc comments of\nmachine_page() and post_section() are above their functions again.\n\nPinned by an_empty_post_folder_shows_the_default_post_as_missing and\na_removed_first_post_is_not_shown_as_another_post.\n\nRefs #2380\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus <noreply@anthropic.com>",
